proof: discimagecreator | fedora | vendor-cap
date: 2026-07-15
lane/VM: test-fedora (Fedora 44 KDE), repo COPR gmipf/media-preservation
user groups: "gmipf wheel" (NO cdrom/disk/plugdev) -> groupless
drive: PLEXTOR DVDR PX-760A (USB) -> /dev/sr1, data CD
mechanism: Fedora %caps(cap_sys_rawio=ep) in discimagecreator.spec

--- delivery ---
$ getcap /usr/libexec/discimagecreator/DiscImageCreator.out
  /usr/libexec/discimagecreator/DiscImageCreator.out cap_sys_rawio=ep
  (DVDAuth.out also carries it)
$ rpm -qf DiscImageCreator.out -> discimagecreator-20260703121302.efa7d482-3.fc44.x86_64

--- GREEN (cap present) ---
$ discimagecreator cd /dev/sr1 /tmp/dic/t.bin 8 /d8
  This drive (DVDR PX-760A ...) supports [OpCode: 0xd8, SubCode: 0]
  ... SubCode: 1 / 2 / 8    # Plextor D8 detected + used
  Creating (Lead-in)(Track 0).scm & .sub ... (LBA) -10000/-10000   # D8 lead-in read
exit 124 (trimmed)

--- RED (setcap -r on DiscImageCreator.out, then restored) ---
$ setcap -r .../DiscImageCreator.out ; getcap -> []
$ discimagecreator cd /dev/sr1 ... /d8
  lpCmd: d8, 00, 00, 00, 00, 00, 00, 00, 00, 01, 02, 00        # the D8 CDB sent
  [F:ExecSearchingOffset][L:190] GetLastError: 1, Operation not permitted
  [F:ReadCDForCheckingSubPack][L:1275] GetLastError: 1, Operation not permitted
  This drive (...PX-760A...) doesn't support [OpCode: 0xd8, SubCode: 2]  # EPERM => "unsupported"
$ setcap cap_sys_rawio=ep .../DiscImageCreator.out -> cap restored

VERDICT: PROVEN. Package-delivered cap_sys_rawio on DiscImageCreator.out is
load-bearing: with it the 0xd8 (>=0xC0) CDB reaches the drive; without it the
identical CDB (lpCmd: d8,...) fails EPERM (kernel gate), and DIC misreads that as
"drive doesn't support 0xd8".
